{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-2029"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Manufacture of other chemical products n.e.c."
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "2029"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :adhesive/structural-bonding
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:worker-safety :consumer-safety :vehicle-safety :supply-resilience]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :bond-strength-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :cae :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies [:cfd :telemetry]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "Adhesive Advisor ⊣ Bond-Strength Governor, langgraph-clj StateGraph,
 MemStore+DatomicStore dual-backend append-only audit ledger. ISIC 2029
 (manufacture of other chemical products n.e.c.) is a residual category;
 this build scopes to ONE concrete, well-justified sub-scope --
 structural adhesives/sealants manufacturing (NOT the whole broad
 category) -- for a manufacturer producing both consumer-electronics-
 grade adhesives (smartphone frame/battery/display bonding, thin-
 bondline) and automotive-grade structural adhesives (body panel
 bonding, battery-pack sealing, crash-durable bond lines). Subject is an
 adhesive-batch. Six ops: `:adhesive-batch/intake` (phase 3 may
 auto-commit when clean), `:bond-standard-rules/verify` (per-product-
 class evidence checklist -- ASTM D1002 / SAE J1836 for automotive
 structural bonding, IPC-CC-830 / UL 746C for electronics-grade
 adhesive-bonded housings -- always human), `:end-of-line-quality/
 screen` (cure-completeness/void/bondline-thickness defect screen, HARD
 unconditional), `:robotics/simulate-lap-shear-test` (a NATIVE real
 physics-2d time-stepped simulation of the ASTM D1002 single-lap-joint
 shear bond-strength test using the collision-as-tension-limit
 reinterpretation technique, always human), and dual actuation
 `:actuation/issue-bond-certificate` / `:actuation/ship-adhesive-batch`
 (both ALWAYS escalate, never auto-eligible at any phase, each with its
 own dedicated boolean guard + append-only history + product-class-
 scoped sequence number; a shipment additionally HARD-requires the bond
 certificate already be on file). Eight concrete governor checks
 elaborate this blueprint's invariants: spec-basis citation, evidence-
 checklist completeness, robotics-simulation missing/independently-out-
 of-tolerance (real ASTM D1002 lap-shear peak force vs. a disclosed
 reasoned-engineering shear-strength band), cure-time-deviation
 out-of-range (two-sided ground-truth range check), certificate-missing-
 before-shipment, end-of-line-defect-unresolved (evaluated
 unconditionally), already-shipped, and already-certified. This is the
 shared upstream structural-adhesives stage feeding BOTH
 cloud-itonami-isic-2630 (smartphone manufacturing) and
 cloud-itonami-isic-2910/-2920 (motor-vehicle manufacturing), with a
 three-way connection into cloud-itonami-isic-2720's battery-pack
 sealing -- the final shared-materials actor closing out this session's
 automotive/smartphone supply-web build-out."}
